[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello.</p>\n<p>The current <code>Repr</code> instance for <code>Vector</code> prints it as a structure. I thought it could instead be made analogous to <code>Array</code>, using a representation close to the literal notation, as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToFormat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">\"#v[]\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bracketFill</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"#v[\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">joinSep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\",\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Format</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"]\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instRepr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">reprPrec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Would it be reasonable to implement this?</p>\n<p>I think this <code>Repr</code> instance should probably be used as the default. What do you think? Would it be appropriate for me to open a PR for this?</p>",
        "id": 608301008,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783266144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure you even need the <code>if</code></p>",
        "id": 608306367,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783271211
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Array.repr also uses this <code>if</code> expression</p>",
        "id": 608306444,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783271288
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One argument against this is that <code>Repr</code> instances are generally supposed to round-trip, i.e,. parseable as a value of the given type, and this would not be the case for your proposed instance:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">irreducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n_eq_0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  #v[]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Vector ?m.5 0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Vector Int n</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608369391,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1783319104
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span> Indeed, an empty Vector cannot be parsed. However, by that argument, wouldn’t an empty Array also be unparseable, since it is displayed as #[]?</p>",
        "id": 608369657,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783319253
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is not about being empty, but about the required size for the vector not being definitionally equal to the number of elements in the literal.</p>",
        "id": 608369878,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1783319365
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see. I’ll think about an appropriate way to address this.</p>",
        "id": 608370151,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783319495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This feels like enough of a corner case to be tolerable; the round tripping is I think only best effort?</p>",
        "id": 608371693,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783320213
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Doesn’t this issue already exist with the current Repr instance as well? It would be nice if we could solve it, but even if we cannot, isn’t it an acceptable limitation?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">irreducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size_toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">don't know how to synthesize placeholder</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">context:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">⊢ #[].size = n</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size_toArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608371769,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783320250
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose <code>#v[a, b, c].cast _</code> is still shorter than the status quo</p>",
        "id": 608371953,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783320351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that the parsing issue should be fixed if possible, but I do not think it is essential. Rather, I think the benefit of displaying vectors in a more readable form outweighs it.</p>",
        "id": 608372185,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1783320472
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span> PR welcome?</p>",
        "id": 611681667,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1784558372
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, go ahead.</p>",
        "id": 611814951,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1784614754
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span> Here is a PR. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14545\">lean4#14545</a></p>",
        "id": 612715796,
        "sender_full_name": "Asei Inoue",
        "timestamp": 1784965305
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This made me realize that the docstring for bracketFill is wrong. it says :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Creates a format `l ++ f ++ r` with a flattening group, nesting the contents by the length of `l`.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">The group's `FlattenBehavior` is `fill`; for `allOrNone` use `Std.Format.bracketFill`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And it should be :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Creates a format `l ++ f ++ r` with a flattening group, nesting the contents by the length of `l`.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">The group's `FlattenBehavior` is `fill`; for `allOrNone` use `Std.Format.bracket`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612727320,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1784977640
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Never mind, it has been fixed in main branch now.</p>",
        "id": 612733142,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1784983969
    }
]